---
title: 15-Minute Creamy Tomato Soup (Vegan)
description: This soup gets a rich, creamy texture from the emulsion of olive oil and bread.
servings: 4
cook time: 15 minutes
time required: 15m
source: https://www.seriouseats.com/15-minute-creamy-tomato-soup-vegan-recipe
author: J. Kenji López-Alt
tags: [soup, vegan, tomato, quick]
---

> This soup gets a rich, creamy texture from the emulsion of olive oil and bread.
> Be careful starting up the blender — the soup can shoot out the top. Open the
> vent and hold a kitchen towel over the lid to prevent blowout.
> You'll also need a @blender{}.

Heat @extra-virgin olive oil{2%tbsp}(divided) in a #large saucepan{} over
medium-high heat until shimmering. Add @garlic{2%cloves}(grated),
@small onion{1}(finely sliced, about 1 cup), @dried oregano{1%tsp}, and
@red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp}. Cook, stirring frequently, until onions are
softened but not browned, about ~{4%minutes}. Add @white bread{2%slices}
(crusts removed, torn into rough 1/2-inch pieces) and @whole peeled tomatoes{56%oz}
(2 28-ounce cans, packed in juice). Roughly mash the tomatoes with a #whisk{} or
a #potato masher{}. Add @water{2%cups}. Bring to a boil over high heat, then
reduce to a simmer. Cook for ~{5%minutes}.

Transfer half of the soup to the jar of a #blender{}. Blend the soup, starting
at low speed and gradually increasing to high. With the blender running on high,
gradually trickle in half of the remaining @extra-virgin olive oil{} (about
2 tbsp). Season the soup to taste with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}.
Transfer to a large bowl and repeat with the remaining half of soup and olive oil.

Ladle into individual serving bowls, top with @minced chives{} (or basil or
parsley), drizzle with more olive oil, and serve with @toasted bread{} or
grilled cheese.

@baking soda{2%tsp} can be used to tame acidity if desired.

-- Nutrition per serving: 324 calories, 23g fat, 26g carbs, 6g protein.
